sentences.t:
Tris Notus abreptas in saxa latentia torquet—
saxa vocant Itali mediis quae in fluctibus aras—
dorsum immane mari summo;

sentences.l:
Three the South Wind, snatched away, onto hidden rocks hurls —
rocks out in mid-waves which the Italians call the Altars —
a huge ridge at the sea's surface;

sentences.t:
Iam validam Ilionei navem, iam fortis Achati,
et qua vectus Abas, et qua grandaevus Aletes,
vicit hiems;

sentences.l:
Now Ilioneus' sturdy ship, now brave Achates',
and the one in which Abas sailed, and the one in which old Aletes,
winter has conquered;

sentences.t:
Interea magno misceri murmure pontum,
emissamque hiemem sensit Neptunus, et imis
stagna refusa vadis, graviter commotus;

sentences.l:
Meanwhile that with great roaring the sea was in turmoil,
and that the storm was let loose, Neptune perceived, and that from the lowest
depths the still waters were poured back up — gravely stirred;

Scattered, Aeneas's fleet over the whole sea he sees,
by the waves overwhelmed the Trojans, and by the sky's collapse;
nor were hidden from her brother the tricks of Juno and her angers.

sentences.t:
Ac veluti magno in populo cum saepe coorta est
seditio, saevitque animis ignobile volgus,
iamque faces et saxa volant—furor arma ministrat;

sentences.l:
And just as in a great people, when, as often, there has arisen
a riot, and rages in its spirits the low-born mob,
and now torches and stones fly — fury supplies the weapons;

sentences.t:
Hinc atque hinc vastae rupes geminique minantur
in caelum scopuli, quorum sub vertice late
aequora tuta silent;

sentences.l:
On this side and that vast cliffs and twin threaten
toward the sky crags, beneath whose summit far and wide
the waters, safe, are silent;

Under the facing front, of hanging rocks, a cave;
within, fresh waters, and of living stone seats,
the home of the nymphs:

sentences.t:
ductoresque ipsos primum, capita alta ferentis
cornibus arboreis, sternit, tum volgus, et omnem
miscet agens telis nemora inter frondea turbam;

